From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:53:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: name the device, timing and GPU error of command queue
 failures

STEAMAC-G: on M3/M4/M5 KosmicKrisp devices are lost with
MTL4CommandQueueErrorTimeout right after Steam's UI starts. 0038's lines
showed no pending semaphore wait; the failed command buffer never started
(M3) or ran 49.9 ms (M5). In 18 of 20 events the error comes 0.3-1.1 s
after Steam's hellovr_vulkan driver probe destroys its device (1.1 s after
gldriverquery's), in one 1.0 s after a window resize.

A command queue error now logs, before the device loss: the command
buffer's number and the guest application of its device (Venus passes
VkApplicationInfo on), how long after its commit it failed, when it
started on the GPU relative to its commit (or that it never started) with
the raw GPU times, when the queue's last completed command buffer ended,
the Metal error's userInfo, the semaphore waits still unsignalled (0038),
the devices alive in the process and the last ones created and destroyed,
and, once per process, the error and fault messages Metal/IOGPU/AGX logged
to os_log in the last 10 s (OSLogStore, current process): Metal 4 reports
page faults, hangs, timeouts and victims of another command buffer's
recovery all as one error code, the IOGPU reason only goes to os_log.
MESA_KK_DEBUG=commits logs device creations/destructions and command
buffers that started 20 ms after their commit, ran 50 ms or completed
100 ms after it.

Feedback handlers now use their queue on every completion, and a handler
could run after vkDeviceWaitIdle, so after vkDestroyDevice: queues count
the commits whose handler has not run and kk_queue_finish waits for them
(it only waited for re-recorded command buffers, whose handler also freed
its data through the device after letting kk_queue_finish go on).
